{"h": {"measure": "R", "k": 100}, "sp": "nb", "rep": 100, "hyps": [{"edit_edge": 2, "edit_op": "nor_conv_3x3", "cond_edge": 2, "cond_op": "none", "direction": "higher", "why": "Adding a conv where there was no node1->node2 connection creates a new learnable path, which gave large gains in #67 and #72."}, {"edit_edge": 3, "edit_op": "nor_conv_3x3", "cond_edge": 4, "cond_op": "none", "direction": "higher", "why": "When edge 1->3 is missing, the direct 0->3 edge carries more of the output, so making it a conv matters more (#86, #17)."}, {"edit_edge": 1, "edit_op": "nor_conv_3x3", "cond_edge": 1, "cond_op": "avg_pool_3x3", "direction": "higher", "why": "Replacing a parameter-free pool with a 3x3 conv on 0->2 adds capacity, giving big gains in #32 vs smaller ones elsewhere."}, {"edit_edge": 5, "edit_op": "none", "cond_edge": 5, "cond_op": "avg_pool_3x3", "direction": "higher", "why": "Removing an avg_pool feeding the output strips harmful smoothing, while removing a conv on that edge loses capacity (#51, #87 vs #36)."}, {"edit_edge": 4, "edit_op": "none", "cond_edge": 5, "cond_op": "none", "direction": "lower", "why": "With 2->3 already absent, removing 1->3 can disconnect the cell's main computational path (#84 collapse)."}, {"edit_edge": 3, "edit_op": "none", "cond_edge": 5, "cond_op": "none", "direction": "lower", "why": "If 2->3 is missing, cutting the direct 0->3 edge leaves too few paths to the output, causing collapse (#50)."}, {"edit_edge": 0, "edit_op": "nor_conv_3x3", "cond_edge": 0, "cond_op": "none", "direction": "higher", "why": "Turning a missing 0->1 edge into a conv activates node 1's downstream edges, giving large gains (#48)."}, {"edit_edge": 4, "edit_op": "avg_pool_3x3", "cond_edge": 4, "cond_op": "nor_conv_3x3", "direction": "lower", "why": "Replacing the strongest op with a parameter-free pool on an output edge loses the most capacity (#74 vs #66)."}, {"edit_edge": 5, "edit_op": "avg_pool_3x3", "cond_edge": 5, "cond_op": "nor_conv_1x1", "direction": 